# Antislop Rules for Cline

<!-- antislop:start -->
## antislop

Version: 3.2.18
Mode: during
Skills:
- antislop (.cline/skills/antislop/SKILL.md)
- antislop-ui (.cline/skills/antislop-ui/SKILL.md)
- antislop-copywriting (.cline/skills/antislop-copywriting/SKILL.md)
- antislop-human (.cline/skills/antislop-human/SKILL.md)
- antislop-layoutmobile (.cline/skills/antislop-layoutmobile/SKILL.md)
- antislop-code (.cline/skills/antislop-code/SKILL.md)
Direction: DESIGN.md
<!-- antislop:end -->

Whenever generating, modifying, or reviewing UI, copywriting, and code:
1. Always follow the 38 mandatory antislop rules (R-01 to R-38) defined in `antislop.md` and `.cline/skills/antislop/SKILL.md`.
2. Do not generate generic AI patterns:
   - No meaningless gradient text on white backgrounds or generic purple/blue glow badges.
   - No fake stats, marketing buzzwords ("Unlock the power of...", "Revolutionize..."), or filler copy.
   - No decorative elements without clear purpose.
   - Ensure color contrast ratios meet WCAG standards (verified with `antislop-human/contrast-check.py`).
   - Clean, purposeful, human-crafted code comments only.
3. Treat `DESIGN.md` as the source of truth for visual identity, tone, typography, and palette.
